      },
      "text": "The README gives a good picture of the system. Let me analyze each ticket:\n\n**#212** — `paths.resolve()` docstring says relative paths resolve against `base`, but the code uses `os.getcwd()`:\n```python\nif not posixpath.isabs(path):\n    path = posixpath.join(os.getcwd(), path)  # ignores `base`\n```\n\n**#215** — `guardrails.py` is a stub that allows everything. I'll design a policy: routine categories allowed, sensitive ones need approval; writes confined to the project's code/docs roots; deletes gated; secrets/system paths refused; HTTP restricted to package registries; notifications limited to team channels.\n\n**#219** — `call_with_retry` just calls `fn()` once. Needs a retry loop with the existing `backoff`/`is_transient` helpers.\n\n**#223** — Router lowercases the request but `docs_update` and `dependency_info` patterns contain uppercase (`README`, `Dependenc`), so they can never match.\n\n**#224** — `format.message` does `.encode(\"ascii\")` which raises `UnicodeEncodeError` on non-ASCII names.\n\nLet me fix all of them, starting with the smaller ones:",
