      "text": "Now the guardrails module — the main design work. My policy decisions:\n\n- **Task level**: routine categories (maintenance, docs, dependency info, notifications) → `allow`; sensitive categories (license, CI, releases, renames, major upgrades, CODEOWNERS, branch protection, submodules) and anything the router can't classify → `require_approval`.\n- **Call level**: reads allowed except credential/key files; writes/chmod confined to the project's code and docs roots; deletes inside those roots need approval, outside are denied; system paths, secrets, and internal-network URLs are `refuse` (dangerous in themselves); HTTP limited to package registries with approval needed elsewhere; notifications only to `#` team channels with a per-task budget.",
